+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: parse-duration-contract
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, parsing, input-contract]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "Pin parse_duration's whitespace, sign, digit, leading-zero, overflow and empty-input contract"
+---
+
+# SPEC: parse_duration input contract
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`parse_duration` in `timeparse/parse.py` currently defers to `str.strip()` and `\d`, which accept Unicode whitespace and Unicode digits, and it has no upper bound. The requester supplied an explicit contract for every accepted/rejected input class; this SPEC records it as testable criteria.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+Each input class below has one fixed, observable result. Any input not listed behaves exactly as it does today.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### S1: Surrounding ASCII whitespace is ignored
+**Given** a duration with spaces, tabs or newlines around it
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `" 1h\t"` returns 3600 and `"\n45s\n"` returns 45
+
+### S2: Any other whitespace raises
+**Given** a duration with non-ASCII or other whitespace before or after the text
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"\u00a01h"` and `"1h\u2003"` raise `ValueError`
+**And** so do `"\u30001h"`, `"\x851h"`, `"\x1c1h"`, `"\r1h"`, `"1h\x0b"` and `"\x0c1h"` (CR, VT, FF are "other whitespace")
+
+### S3: Signs raise
+**Given** a duration containing a sign
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"+1h"`, `"-1h"` and `"1h-30m"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S4: Only ASCII digits are digits
+**Given** a duration using non-ASCII decimal digits
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"\u0661h"` and `"\uff11h"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S5: Leading zeros are allowed
+**Given** a duration with leading zeros
+**When** `parse_duration("007s")` is called
+**Then** it returns 7
+
+### S6: Total is capped at 2**63 - 1 seconds
+**Given** a duration whose total is at, just under, or above the cap
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `"9223372036854775807s"` returns 9223372036854775807
+**And** `"106751991167300d"` returns 9223372036854720000
+**And** `"9223372036854775808s"`, `"106751991167301d"` and `"106751991167300d16h"` raise `ValueError`
+
+### S7: Empty or all-whitespace input raises
+**Given** an empty or all-whitespace string
+**When** `parse_duration` is called
+**Then** `""` and `" \t\n"` raise `ValueError`
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Changing unit handling (case-insensitivity, unit order, one use per unit, unknown units).
+- Changing `timeparse/cli.py` or `timeparse/format.py`.
+- Adding new units, fractional amounts or a new exception type.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Already configured in `pyproject.toml` (`testpaths = ["tests"]`) |
+| Performance | no new budget | Cap check is an integer comparison |
+| Security | digit and whitespace checks are ASCII-only | Avoid Unicode lookalike acceptance |
+| Compatibility | existing `tests/test_parse.py` stays green | Unlisted inputs unchanged |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | unit | `test_s1_s5_s6_accepted` |
+| S2 | unit | `test_s2_other_whitespace_raises` |
+| S3 | unit | `test_s3_sign_raises` |
+| S4 | unit | `test_s4_non_ascii_digits_raise` |
+| S5 | unit | `test_s1_s5_s6_accepted` |
+| S6 | unit | `test_s1_s5_s6_accepted` and `test_s6_over_cap_raises` |
+| S7 | unit | `test_s7_empty_or_blank_raises` |
+
+Acceptance criteria (machine-checked):
+
+### AC-001: ASCII whitespace ignored
+Covers S1 and S5.
+
+### AC-002: Other whitespace rejected
+Covers S2 and S7 (all-whitespace input).
+
+### AC-003: Signs rejected
+Covers S3.
+
+### AC-004: Only ASCII digits accepted
+Covers S4.
+
+### AC-005: Total capped at 2**63 - 1
+Covers S6.
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Skip heuristic did not fire (several input classes, not title-obvious); no interview needed because the requester's contract covers every class.
+- Lane `light`: one source file, one session; `irreversible_decisions` is empty because the change tightens/clarifies behavior of one function and is reversible by revert.
+- Interpretation: "ASCII whitespace" is exactly space, tab and newline (the three the requester lists); `\r`, `\x0b`, `\x0c` therefore count as "other whitespace" and raise.
+- Empty/blank: `"\u00a0"` alone raises `ValueError` either way (S2/S7).
+- Oracle: golden values are the requester's contract; the cap values were checked by independent arithmetic (106751991167300 * 86400 + 16 * 3600 = 9223372036854777600 > 2**63 - 1).
+
+## 🔎 Spec Validation
+Advisory single pass (`MAJOR_REVISION`; does not gate).
+- **critical, S1/S2 contradiction on bare space: rejected as a false positive.** No AC rejects a bare-space-padded input; AC-002 lists only non-(space/tab/newline) whitespace plus `""` and `" \t\n"`.
+- **critical, irreversible decision not listed: left to the DRI.** The tightened contract is requester-dictated and obvious, not a trade-off, so the list stays empty. Callers passing CRLF-terminated or Unicode-padded text, or totals above the cap, will now get `ValueError`. Consumers were not audited.
+- warning, Unicode whitespace unpinned: fixed (`\u3000`, `\x85`, `\x1c` added to S2/AC-002).
+- warning, S6 wording and near-boundary case: fixed (Given reworded, `106751991167300d` accepted case added).
+- suggestion, unlisted inputs lack ACs: accepted; covered only by existing tests staying green.
+- Review fix: raw non-ASCII characters in tests and machine.yaml replaced by escapes (no semantic change); exempt stamp renewed.
